{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Captain America, Living Legend — Azorius Free-Crew Vehicles",
  "format": "commander",
  "description": "**The engine:** every creature you control gets \"the first time it becomes tapped during your\nturn, untap it\" (CR 603.2e — cause-agnostic, so cost-taps count). That erases every tap cost in\nthe deck: Crew is free and your blockers stay up, Station fires TWICE per creature per turn,\nevery mana dork taps for double, convoke and improvise cost nothing, and the whole team gets\npseudo-vigilance (CR 508.2b puts the untap before blockers; CR 506.4b keeps them attacking).\n\n**Two limits that shape the list.** (1) The trigger says \"during your turn\" — Cap does NOTHING\non opponents' turns, so the deck must be proactive, and untappers that work on their turns\n(Lita, Unwinding Clock effects) are covering a real hole. (2) The untap always resolves AFTER\nthe spell/ability that caused the tap is fully cast (CR 601.2i → 603.3), so the bonus mana can\nnever pay for the spell that generated it — tap with priority first, then cast.\n\nGrounds: `research/decisions.md`.",
